.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1045 AM PDT Sun Sep 6 2026

VFR as low stratus has cleared the Bay Area terminals and fog
dissipated across the North Bay. Expect west to northwesterly
winds to increase late this morning and more so by the afternoon
before easing after sunset. Low to moderate confidence of stratus
returning tonight into Monday morning. VFR conditions return by
late Monday morning once any low clouds that do develop dissipate
and give way to sunny sky conditions. Onshore winds also increase
by Monday afternoon.

Vicinity of SFO...VFR. High confidence for VFR conditions to
prevail through the evening with increasing onshore winds with
gusts up to 25 kt this afternoon. Winds ease a bit late in the
evening with the potential for MVFR CIGs to return early Monday
morning, however confidence is low to moderate (20-45% probability
based off of the NBM). Any low CIGs that do develop will
dissipate by around 16Z-17Z Monday with VFR conditions returning
and increasing onshore winds.

SFO Bridge Approach...Similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...VFR. Onshore winds increase this
afternoon and early evening before diminishing after sunset. There
is a 20-55% probability of seeing MVFR conditions returning after
09Z Monday and 30-40% of IFR conditions between 10Z-16Z. Thus,
have introduced IFR/MVFR CIGs around 12-17Z.

