.BEACHES...
Issued at 538 PM PDT Sat Sep 5 2026

A Beach Hazards Statement is in effect through Labor Day as the
swell from tropical cyclones Marie and Karina reach the coast.
Waves from these cyclones will travel over 1,000 miles in all
directions, gradually flattening out to low amplitude, but long
period swell. These waves aren`t very intimidating if you`re on a
boat in the open ocean, but the long period allows them to push
much farther up the beach. Long period swell always increases the
chance for sneaker waves, but that`s particularly true this
weekend since there are 2 different sets of southerly swell, and
their energy will periodically combine. In addition to sneaker
waves, expect strong rip currents and breaking waves up to 10 ft.
As this is a holiday weekend and the weather is otherwise pretty
nice, the exposure to the risk is high. Avoid the water if you`re
not an expert swimmer. If caught in a rip current, swim parallel
to shore until you stop feeling the pull. Even on the beach, be
prepared for sneaker waves this weekend and never turn your back
on the ocean.

